--- body ---

## Context

The Exp 2 smoke (ticket 0185) currently asks Phase A to design only
`designed_prompt` (user-side text) and `settings`
(thinking, max_tokens). The **system prompt** is left untouched —
it's whatever each adapter's default agent description carries
(Mistral: `"AEDIST SOTA experiment agent with web_search connector."`).

The §4 manuscript prose says

> "we give each model our complete prompt and the quality criteria
> above, and ask it to tune **the prompt and settings**"

The plural "prompt" is naturally read as both system and user.
Leaving the system prompt fixed is leaving a strong lever on the
table — system prompts often steer behaviour more than user prompts.

Author quality-review (2026-05-21) of the turn-1 inventory flagged
this explicitly: per-row source columns came back empty even
though the original `prompt_complete.txt` asks for per-cell
sourcing. A designed system prompt could enforce that behaviourally
("you MUST populate every Source 1 and Source 2 cell") in a way that
user-side instructions alone don't always survive.

## Per-adapter system-prompt surface

| Adapter | Where the system prompt lives |
|---|---|
| Mistral Agents | `POST /v1/agents` body `description` field |
| Anthropic | `messages.create` `system` parameter |
| OpenAI Responses | `instructions` parameter on `responses.create` |
| Qwen DashScope | `messages[0]` with `role: "system"` |

## Actions

1. Extend the Phase A JSON envelope spec (in
   `experiments/sota/exp2_interactive_smoke.py::assemble_meta_prompt`)
   to include a fourth required key: `system_prompt` (string).
2. Update `extract_phase_a_design` to require the new key
   (existing tolerant-JSON parsing already handles arbitrary keys).
3. Thread `design["system_prompt"]` into Mistral's `agent_create`
   body's `description` field via a new `system_prompt` kwarg on
   `adapter_mistral.run()` (multi-turn-start mode only — follow-up
   turns reuse the agent).
4. Document the per-adapter surface (above) in a docstring near
   the kwarg so the other three adapters get the same treatment
   when extended.
5. Tests:
   - `test_extract_phase_a_design_requires_system_prompt_key`
   - `test_assemble_meta_prompt_announces_system_prompt_field`
   - `test_adapter_mistral_system_prompt_threads_to_agent_description`
     (mock httpx; verify agent_create body has the right
     description field)
6. Re-smoke Mistral with the extended envelope.

## Invariants

- Backward compatibility: if Phase A doesn't return a
  `system_prompt` key (older saved designs), the smoke must fall
  back to the adapter's default and log the fallback.
- The system prompt is a string only — no nested structure (don't
  invite Mistral to return a dict for it, per the dict-vs-string
  finding from earlier 0185 runs).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Phase A envelope spec includes `system_prompt`
- [ ] Mistral adapter accepts a `system_prompt` kwarg in
      multi-turn-start mode
- [ ] Per-adapter system-prompt surface documented
- [ ] Re-smoke produces an inventory where per-row source columns
      are no longer empty (or, if still empty, we have data showing
      it's a model-skill issue not a prompt-design issue)
